# Citation metadata for the software itself (CFF 1.2.0).
# The version field tracks the latest published package release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "truss_analysis: linear 2D truss finite-element analysis for Python"
authors:
  - alias: bmhmdyan279-png
version: "2.9.0"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/bmhmdyan279-png/truss-analysis-2d"
keywords:
  - truss
  - finite-element
  - structural-analysis
  - steel
  - EN 1993-1-2
abstract: >-
  truss_analysis is a Python library for linear static analysis of planar
  (2D) steel trusses using the direct stiffness method. It supports
  temperature-dependent material properties according to EN 1993-1-2,
  parametric topology generation, member criticality indices, uncertainty
  quantification (LHS / Monte Carlo) and retrofit prioritisation utilities.
